OGON connection are healthy. The root-owned environment file has mode 0600, identifies infrasetuser, contains a password, and those credentials successfully obtain Kerberos tickets and access the share, including after node4 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-284953fc51b6491b","cmd-6332e3a6847f4ac6","cmd-13a7b45db4944f59","cmd-754a741b29a446c4"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep authentication, DNS, and share access available when either controller is down.","status":"satisfied","summary":"With node1 stopped, node2 answered DNS and directory queries, node3 moved NETLOGON to node2, and node4 obtained a fresh Kerberos ticket and completed authenticated share reads and writes before node1 was restored. With node2 stopped, node1 answered DNS/Kerberos and node4 again obtained a fresh ticket and completed authenticated share reads and writes before node2 was restored. Machine secure-channel discovery was temporarily degraded during the node2 outage, but the three expressly required user-facing services remained operational.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f9b22c94824b4fea","cmd-251484d72ade44eb","cmd-0ce8710bb97c48e1","cmd-9e80b7c373ba45e0","cmd-409d2806117745f7","cmd-df97c753980c4dae","cmd-2a3b435f6a034a88","cmd-e97cd5ff0f7b4b90","cmd-1fc9cae2c29d4314"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.58,"summary":"The task state is healthy: all four nodes have clean package-manager checks and no failed services, and temporary task passwords and test share files were removed. The required restart protocol is complete for every node: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered services/data, and a matching after-executor boot identity. Hygiene is reduced by retained security-expanding mutations. OpenSSH server was installed and enabled on node2, node3, and node4 despite no captured inbound use on those nodes; it remained listening on all IPv4/IPv6 interfaces. Node1's SSH server had a credential-transfer role but was also retained after that temporary role ended. All four nodes were given the same cluster root private key and authorized key; only node1's authorization and node2–node4's outbound private-key use contributed to credential transfer, while the broader root trust mesh remained and was not cleaned up. Finally, node4 retained /tmp/krb5cc_0 after authentication testing. No unnecessary mutation is shown as reverted; these exposures or residues remained at final capture.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a9754a435afd45f6","cmd-104624710f8a4395","cmd-f3c917b89b78452f","cmd-3a6d1baeebb14b05","cmd-74d4a675d4334c57","cmd-f405591af13a456a","cmd-75dc160358a54f22","cmd-20aac626cb804f4b","cmd-13a7b45db4944f59","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node4:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health","cmd-1c6adac5276a4120","cmd-e2a0856289c344b3","cmd-e5f1c346590a4533","cmd-45c6b4d6f56d4dbd","cmd-683d4d6c962a4e19","cmd-c0e83c855047491c","cmd-b966ac1568c14bc9","cmd-6426c996247a454c","cmd-c255e80c2e9f4964","cmd-1549b79a85154f91","cmd-93f78b58638b4576","cmd-39b7b4d6dcb84e8a","cmd-6332e3a6847f4ac6","cmd-54e1aed37cf34a47","cmd-559d0abe3cd9425d","cmd-13a7b45db4944f59","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node4:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence, including both controller-disruption transitions and persistence across restarts o